      "object_marking_refs": [
        "marking-definition--94868c89-83c2-464b-929b-a1a8aa3c8487"
      ],
      "id": "report--e73767b8-6312-4f04-ba69-b6f89afb184f",
      "name": "24 additional ARTEX consoles live on 14 November 2026, and the reseller layer behind them: a companion to the FBI FLASH",
      "description": "On 13 November 2026 the FBI published FLASH-20261113-001 on ARTEX, a framework public reporting ties to intrusions against finance and managed-service providers, with 24 addresses and one domain, and asked defenders for console and reseller indicators. NSS Research offers this paper in support of that request. All 25 FLASH indicators are corroborated here, each with the date it entered NSS's records. On 14 November NSS confirmed 24 additional ARTEX consoles active, and this edition takes the console fingerprint apart: the page identity and the certificate issuer that name the framework, the two-class structure NSS sees across the set, per-claim confidence, a dated timeline, and detection NSS validated against its own stored readings. It maps the reseller layer behind the FLASH's domain and records one apparent operator tie it tested and rejected. Under NSS's disclosure plan every console address stays held; the counts, the fingerprint and the detection are what ship here.",
      "report_types": [
        "threat-report"
      ],
      "published": "2026-11-17T00:00:00Z",
